### Bug Scenario and Root Cause

The issue described in the bug report is that the `ol.select.Interaction` feature is always rendered on top of other layers, regardless of the `zIndex` setting. The images provided show that the red dots, which simulate a 'hover' effect, are rendered below the selected feature, even though they are in a separate layer.

The root cause of this issue is likely related to how the `zIndex` is being handled for the select interaction layer. The `Select` interaction uses an unmanaged layer for selected features, and this layer might be set to always render on top, ignoring the `zIndex` settings of other layers.

### Bug Location

The relevant code is in the `src/ol/layer/Layer.js` file, specifically in the `setMap` method. This method sets the `zIndex` of the unmanaged layer to `Infinity`, which causes it to always render on top.

### Patch to Fix the Bug

To fix this issue, we need to modify the `setMap` method in `src/ol/layer/Layer.js` to respect the `zIndex` setting provided in the options, rather than setting it to `Infinity`.

